  "commit_context": "Measured base commit, with the then-uncommitted benchmark. Benchmark source and results are published in the commit that adds this file.",
  "catchup_limits": "Serial, one request in flight. The 2,000-record case makes 1,807 requests: 1 head GET, 1 pending GET, 5 change-feed pages of 500 entries, and 1,800 record GETs. The fixture device already holds all authority and blob chunks and 10% of operation records; a genuinely new device must fetch every record and every blob chunk, making more requests. At 60 ms round trip, 1,807 * 0.060 s = 108.42 s (about 108 s) of latency alone, or about 126 s with the measured local work. This was not measured over a network. SDK exchanges stop a pass after 180 seconds, so a new device joining a 100,000-record library over a real network needs more than one pass.",
